    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#import libraries\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns"
      ],
      "id": "f35b87ba",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Importing the data\n",
        "# need to use the data that is in the github repo already\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Data-Science-Capstone-Project-2026/Capstone2026-Applicant-Trajectory/refs/heads/main/data/processed/capstone_data_processed.csv?token=GHSAT0AAAAAAD6EU5X5Y7RBSNNASAI2C2VK2SS7PKA\")"
      ],
      "id": "0156bd19",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "```{r}\n",
        "library(tidyverse)\n",
        "df = read_csv(\"C:\\\\Users\\\\cocom\\\\Downloads\\\\capstone_data_processed.csv\")\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data Exploration\n",
        "This is a print-out of the columns, what they are, and what they represent. \n",
        "\n",
        "The columns that represent our target variables are \n",
        "- is_nw5\n",
        "- is_large_public\n",
        "- dest_other\n",
        "\n",
        "These three columns are all booleans, with a 1 representing a truth and a zero representing false. Each row should have 1 out of the three columns that have a 1, and the other two columns should have a zero, since a school can either be a NW5 school, a large public school, or another type of school. \n",
        "\n",
        "This cell confirms that there are no instances in which a person attends a school that is marked as multiple of the school types. "
      ],
      "id": "369df666"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df.loc[((df['is_nw5']==1) & (df['is_large_public']==1)) | ((df['is_nw5']==1) & (df['dest_other'] == 1)) | ((df['is_large_public']==1) & df['dest_other']==1) | (df['dest_other']==1)& (df['is_nw5']==1) & (df['is_large_public']==1)]"
      ],
      "id": "892ebc7c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df.head()\n",
        "#df.names()"
      ],
      "id": "591c459b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Distribution of Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "This section will look at the distribution of variables faceted by NW5 school, large public school, or another type of school.\n"
      ],
      "id": "f8bf074b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "g=sns.pairplot(df, diag_kind='kde')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "237bf3f5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Categorical Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Geography\n",
        "\n",
        "Within each student's application, we have access to information about where they lived when they applied to Willamette.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "# graph of where students are from by region\n",
        "place_df = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        n_region = case_when(\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('CA', 'WA', 'OR') ~ \"West Coast\",\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AZ', 'NV', 'NM', 'TX' ) ~ 'Southwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ID', 'MT', 'UT', 'WY', 'CO') ~ 'Rocky Mtn',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ND', 'SD', 'NE', 'KS', 'OK', 'MN', 'IA', 'MO', 'IL', 'OH', 'MI', 'WI', 'IN' ) ~ 'Midwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('MA', 'VT', 'MA', 'NH', 'NY', 'RI', 'NJ', 'CT', 'DE', 'MD', 'PA', 'DC') ~ 'Northeast',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AR', 'AL', 'LA', 'MS', 'GA', 'SC', 'NC', 'VA', 'WV', 'KY', 'TN', 'FL') ~ 'South',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c(\"AK\", 'HI') ~ 'AK/HI',\n",
        "            (is.na(active_region) & active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_country)) | (active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_region)) ~ 'International') ) %>%\n",
        "            select('school_loc', 'n_region', 'active_region', 'active_country') %>%\n",
        "        drop_na(n_region)\n",
        "  #print(place_df)\n",
        "ggplot(data=place_df, aes(x=fct_rev(fct_infreq(n_region)))) + geom_bar() +coord_flip() +labs(\n",
        "  title=\"Region of Origin for Applicants\",\n",
        "  y = 'Number of Applicants',\n",
        "  x = 'Applicant Region of Origin'\n",
        ")+ geom_text(stat = \"count\", aes(label = after_stat(count)), hjust = -.23)\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "# split by region including other by count\n",
        "place_df = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        n_region = case_when(\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('CA', 'WA', 'OR') ~ \"West Coast\",\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AZ', 'NV', 'NM', 'TX' ) ~ 'Southwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ID', 'MT', 'UT', 'WY', 'CO') ~ 'Rocky Mtn',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ND', 'SD', 'NE', 'KS', 'OK', 'MN', 'IA', 'MO', 'IL', 'OH', 'MI', 'WI', 'IN' ) ~ 'Midwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('MA', 'VT', 'MA', 'NH', 'NY', 'RI', 'NJ', 'CT', 'DE', 'MD', 'PA', 'DC') ~ 'Northeast',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AR', 'AL', 'LA', 'MS', 'GA', 'SC', 'NC', 'VA', 'WV', 'KY', 'TN', 'FL') ~ 'South',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c(\"AK\", 'HI') ~ 'AK/HI',\n",
        "            (is.na(active_region) & active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_country)) | (active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_region)) ~ 'International')\n",
        "        )  %>% drop_na(n_region)\n",
        "ggplot(data=place_df, aes(x=n_region, fill=school_loc)) + geom_bar(stat=\"count\", position=\"dodge\") \n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "# graph of percentages of students split by region attending each type of school\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        n_region = case_when(\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('CA', 'WA', 'OR') ~ \"West Coast\",\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AZ', 'NV', 'NM', 'TX' ) ~ 'Southwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ID', 'MT', 'UT', 'WY', 'CO') ~ 'Rocky Mtn',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ND', 'SD', 'NE', 'KS', 'OK', 'MN', 'IA', 'MO', 'IL', 'OH', 'MI', 'WI', 'IN' ) ~ 'Midwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('MA', 'VT', 'MA', 'NH', 'NY', 'RI', 'NJ', 'CT', 'DE', 'MD', 'PA', 'DC') ~ 'Northeast',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AR', 'AL', 'LA', 'MS', 'GA', 'SC', 'NC', 'VA', 'WV', 'KY', 'TN', 'FL') ~ 'South',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c(\"AK\", 'HI') ~ 'AK/HI',\n",
        "            (is.na(active_region) & active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_country)) | (active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_region)) ~ 'International')\n",
        "        ) %>% drop_na(n_region, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(n_region, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1)\n",
        "        \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=n_region, y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "This graph shows us that \n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "# graph of percentages of students who go to either large public or nw5, not other. split by region\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        n_region = case_when(\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('CA', 'WA', 'OR') ~ \"West Coast\",\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AZ', 'NV', 'NM', 'TX' ) ~ 'Southwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ID', 'MT', 'UT', 'WY', 'CO') ~ 'Rocky Mtn',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('ND', 'SD', 'NE', 'KS', 'OK', 'MN', 'IA', 'MO', 'IL', 'OH', 'MI', 'WI', 'IN' ) ~ 'Midwest',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('MA', 'VT', 'MA', 'NH', 'NY', 'RI', 'NJ', 'CT', 'DE', 'MD', 'PA', 'DC') ~ 'Northeast',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c('AR', 'AL', 'LA', 'MS', 'GA', 'SC', 'NC', 'VA', 'WV', 'KY', 'TN', 'FL') ~ 'South',\n",
        "            active_region %in% c(\"AK\", 'HI') ~ 'AK/HI',\n",
        "            (is.na(active_region) & active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_country)) | (active_country != 'United States' & !is.na(active_region)) ~ 'International')\n",
        "        ) %>% drop_na(n_region, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(n_region, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=n_region, y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col(position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"Applicant Region of Origin\",\n",
        "      y = \"Perentage of Students per Region\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "From this graph, we can see that\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Financials\n",
        "\n",
        "The cost to attend college can be quite large, especially going to a NW5 school instead of a large public school. This has the potential to be a large factor in where students decide to attend. \n",
        "It could also be interesting to look at if students are first generation and if they tend to go to a certain type of school, potentially one with less overall cost to them and their families. \n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Columns to look at:\n",
        "common_app_fee_waiver - could be null or zero even if they would receive financial aid, but they applied to schools that did not have an application fee\n",
        "need_based_aid - could be indicative of a person who would have to pay attention to total cost before they choose a school.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df %>% filter('need_based_aid' != 0) %>% select('need_based_aid', 'talent_scholarships', 'efc_sai', 'common_app_fee_waiver')\n",
        "```\n",
        "Based on the columns that are null and active, we will look at the potential correlation between need based aid and destination, as well as common_app_fee_waiver and destination.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(need_based_aid, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(need_based_aid, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE))\n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          #filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=as.factor(need_based_aid), y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    scale_x_discrete(labels = c(\"0\" = \"Not Eligible\", \"1\" = \"Eligible\")) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"Eligibility of Need Based Aid\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(need_based_aid, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(need_based_aid, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE)) %>%\n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=as.factor(need_based_aid), y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    scale_x_discrete(labels = c(\"0\" = \"Not Eligible\", \"1\" = \"Eligible\")) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"Eligibility of Need Based Aid\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "From this graph, we can see that based on the eligibility of need based aid, there is not really a relationship bewteen just the eligibility of need based aid and going to a large public school or a NW5 school. \n",
        "\n",
        "#### Demographics\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "This graph is mostly going to look at the first-generation status of students\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(first_gen_status, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(first_gen_status, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE)) %>%\n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=as.factor(first_gen_status), y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    scale_x_discrete(labels = c(\"0\" = \"Not First Generation\", \"1\" = \"First Generation\")) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"First Generation Status\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(first_gen_status, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(first_gen_status, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE)) \n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          #filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=as.factor(first_gen_status), y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    scale_x_discrete(labels = c(\"0\" = \"Not First Generation\", \"1\" = \"First Generation\")) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"First Generation Status\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Learned from first-gen graphs:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Race/Ethnicity\n",
        "column: ipeds_classification\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "unique(df['ipeds_classification'])\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(ipeds_classification, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(ipeds_classification, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE)) \n",
        "\n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=ipeds_classification, y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"Ethnicity of Student\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9)) +\n",
        "      theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 45, vjust = 1, hjust = 1))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{r}\n",
        "df_loc = df %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = case_when(\n",
        "        is_nw5==1 ~ \"NW 5\",\n",
        "        is_large_public==1 ~ \"Large Public\",\n",
        "        dest_other==1 ~ \"Other\"\n",
        "        )) %>% \n",
        "    drop_na(ipeds_classification, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    group_by(ipeds_classification, school_loc) %>% \n",
        "    summarise(subtotal = n(), .groups = \"drop_last\") %>% \n",
        "    mutate(total_by_var1 = sum(subtotal),\n",
        "          percent = subtotal/total_by_var1) %>%\n",
        "    mutate(school_loc = fct_reorder(school_loc, percent, .fun = identity, .desc=TRUE)) %>%\n",
        "          #filtering out the \"other schools\"\n",
        "          filter(school_loc == 'Large Public' | school_loc == 'NW 5') \n",
        "    print(df_loc)\n",
        "    ggplot(data=df_loc,aes(x=ipeds_classification, y=percent,fill=school_loc)) + geom_col( position=\"dodge\") +\n",
        "    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +\n",
        "    labs (\n",
        "      x= \"Ethnicity of Student\",\n",
        "      y = \"Percentage of Students\",\n",
        "      fill = \"Attended School Category\"\n",
        "      )+ geom_text(aes(label = round(percent*100,2)), vjust = -.5, position = position_dodge(width=0.9)) +\n",
        "      theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 45, vjust = 1, hjust = 1))\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Academics\n",
        "Mostly interested in GPA, test scores, academic rigor, writing rating. Do more academically successful students tend to go private or public?\n",
        "\n",
        "Academic columns:\n",
        "app_weighted_gpa\n",
        "app_unweighted_gpa\n",
        "app_transfer_gpa\n",
        "co_curricular_rating (1-6) 6 most demanding\n",
        "curriculum_rating (1-6) 6 most demanding\n",
        "writing_rating (1-4) 4 outstanding\n",
        "converted_satr_superscore\n",
        "person_calculated_merit_rank (num scale)\n",
